> > is a linguistic rule that says "the sense of word X = the sense of word
> > Y". I have such a rule for 'Wolfram' and 'Tungsten'. If you lack such a
> > rule, then X and Y aren't synonyms, even though their senses may be
> > extensionally equivalent
>
> Most Americans don't know the word Wolfram, so they can't know whether or not
> it is a synonym for Tungsten.

Ergo most Americans don't believe that _wolfram_ and _tungsten_ are
synonyms.

> Ingorance has nothing to do with belief, or
> with the meanings of the words

I would have thought ignorance has a great deal to do with belief,
and with the meanings of words.

